From 5e47b7603d11eef20e08cbe0de413c33a8dec0e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: palazik <gochmyradov0@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:20:19 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] dodge: fix the framebuffer block descriptor's output address

The splash framebuffer block OR-ed 0xfc800000 straight into the L2 block
descriptor. With 16K pages an L2 block is 32MB and the descriptor's
output address field is bits[47:25], so the framebuffer's 8MB offset into
its block landed on bit 23 - inside the RES0 field [24:17]. A descriptor
with RES0 bits set is CONSTRAINED UNPREDICTABLE and a core may take a
translation fault on it.

Map the containing block, 0xfc000000, which covers the framebuffer and
leaves the reserved bits clear. The L2 index is unchanged (126 either
way), so the mapping is the same identity mapping, now well-formed.

Nothing had exercised this entry before: every stripe up to the MMU
switch is a plain physical store with translation still off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 osfmk/arm64/start.s | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/start.s b/osfmk/arm64/start.s
index 589dcc2..7dbfc0a 100644
--- a/osfmk/arm64/start.s
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/start.s
@@ -660,8 +660,15 @@ Lkernelcache_base_found:
 	 * create_bootstrap_mapping would replace the RAM L2 table.
 	 * DODGE uses 16K pages and all bring-up RAM is below 4GB, so the first
 	 * V=P L2 page is bootstrap_pagetables + 2*PGBYTES.
+	 *
+	 * Map the whole 32MB block the framebuffer lives in, 0xfc000000, not
+	 * 0xfc800000: a block descriptor's output address field is bits[47:25],
+	 * and the framebuffer sits 8MB into its block, so OR-ing its address in
+	 * would have set bit 23 inside the descriptor's RES0 field [24:17].
+	 * That is CONSTRAINED UNPREDICTABLE and a core is allowed to take a
+	 * translation fault on it, which is exactly what this store must not do.
 	 */
-	MOV64	x10, 0xfc800000
+	MOV64	x10, 0xfc000000
 	MOV64	x11, (ARM_TTE_TYPE_BLOCK | ARM_TTE_VALID | ARM_TTE_BLOCK_SH(SH_OUTER_MEMORY) | ARM_TTE_BLOCK_ATTRINDX(CACHE_ATTRINDX_WRITECOMB) | ARM_TTE_BLOCK_AF | ARM_TTE_BLOCK_PNX | ARM_TTE_BLOCK_NX)
 	orr		x11, x11, x10
 	and		x12, x10, #(ARM_TT_L2_INDEX_MASK)
